--- Zefram <zefram@fysh.org> wrote:
> Until now it is always legal to pause at any word break.  If a pause
> is to become significant there then "ybu" must become a single word so
> that it is not permitted to pause in the middle of it. 

That's a good point. Yes, {ybu} as a separate word (of selmaho BY)
makes sense. 

> That doesn't
> introduce any ambiguity, but does complicate the morphology.

Not that much. {y} and {y'y} are already exceptional words each in 
a class of their own, they are the only words in the language
that begin with y, so having a third one {ybu} would not be such 
a big deal. The slight complication in morphology would
be compensated by the great simplification in syntax. 
{y} becomes transparent to everything, and {ybu} is just
another member of an already existing selma'o.

> I think I'd better do a proper analysis of the morphology, soon, before
> it gets any more complicated.

Good!

